  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TCPF: Inclusive agri-therapeutic approaches for livelihoods and vulnerable youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To establish inclusive agriculture-based rehabilitation and livelihood options by piloting an agri-therapeutic model that supports functional recovery, psychosocial well-being, and reintegration into productive agrifood activities for persons with disabilities, particularly stroke survivors.
Strengthen inclusive skills development, agri-entrepreneurship, and employment opportunities for persons with disabilities, youth, and caregivers through adapted training, assistive tools, and market-linked livelihood models that improves household resilience and economic participation.
Generate evidence and strengthen systems for disability-inclusive agrifood programming by documenting lessons, building partnerships, and informing policies and programmes to mainstream disability inclusion within agricultural extension, rehabilitation services, and agrifood investment initiatives aligned with national priorities.</narrative>
  </description>
